.ipynb_checkpoints/
.virtual_documents/
data/LIST_v1-2.parquet

# Per-iteration raw simulation results (>100 MB, exceeds GitHub limit).
# Reconstructable deterministically from seed_hex; live copies on sapphire +
# archive to Zenodo at paper submission per GH issue #3 (Phase 2 reproducibility).
# Summary parquets (cell-summary, thresholds, power-curves) ARE committed.
runs/**/cell-results.parquet
runs/**/run.pid

# Recovery-grid state file — RULE (defined 2026-06-08, Shawn): grid-state.json is
# a LIVE orchestration file (rewritten continuously during a run, goes stale, and
# collides on concurrent pulls), so it is NOT tracked. The committed run record is
# grid-state-final.json — a run-close snapshot (`cp grid-state.json
# grid-state-final.json`) — alongside REPORT.md + tables/. grid-state-final.json
# is NOT matched by the pattern below and stays tracked.
runs/**/grid-state.json

# Recovery-grid two-unit re-simulation (2026-05-26): production
# per-replicate synthetic data (45,000 / grid) and per-replicate posterior
# fits (45,000 / grid) regenerate deterministically from base_seed +
# cell_index + replicate; bulk would push the repo past the GitHub limit.
# grid-state-final.json (run-close snapshot), REPORT.md, and tables/grid-summary.parquet ARE committed (live grid-state.json is ignored — see the rule near the top).
# Per-cell summary JSONs are NOT committed (Shawn 2026-06-03): their content is
# preserved compactly in tables/grid-summary.parquet, so the 450 redundant JSONs
# per grid are gitignored below. A 5-replicate fixture of the smoke-test cell
# (shape=rise_and_fall_alpha=0.50_tier=uniform_N=2000 — replicates 000-004 of the
# synthetic data + cell-fits, plus the cell-summary) is ALREADY committed as the
# research record of the pre-launch gates; those tracked files stay tracked. The
# full-run overflow (replicates 005+) and every other cell are regenerable from
# the deterministic synth.py and are ignored (2026-06-14: dropped the
# whole-cell re-includes so the overflow no longer shows as untracked).
runs/2026-05-26-recovery-grid-two-unit/*/data/synthetic-cells/*/
runs/2026-05-26-recovery-grid-two-unit/*/outputs/cell-fits/*/
runs/2026-05-26-recovery-grid-two-unit/*/outputs/cell-logs/
runs/2026-05-26-recovery-grid-two-unit/*/outputs/cell-summaries/*
!runs/2026-05-26-recovery-grid-two-unit/*/outputs/cell-summaries/shape=rise_and_fall_alpha=0.50_tier=uniform_N=2000-summary.json

# Diagnostic-run NUTS logs + regenerable scratch synth (results CSV/parquet/PNG
# ARE committed; the verbose sampler logs and scratch are not).
runs/2026-06-02-recovery-utility-check/outputs/*.log
runs/2026-06-03-small-n-reachability/outputs/*.log
# Checkpoint log (operational; identical records to the committed replicates.parquet).
runs/2026-06-03-small-n-reachability/outputs/*.jsonl
runs/2026-06-03-small-n-reachability/outputs/scratch/
# 2026-06-04 finer-alpha envelope run (results CSV/parquet committed; logs/jsonl/scratch not).
runs/2026-06-04-envelope-finer-alpha/outputs/*.log
runs/2026-06-04-envelope-finer-alpha/outputs/*.jsonl
runs/2026-06-04-envelope-finer-alpha/outputs/scratch/

# Intermediate filtered LIRE corpora (~ 60 MB each). Reconstructable from the
# original LIRE_v3-0.parquet via the run's filter script. Live on sapphire too
# when blocks run there; pulled back as needed.
runs/**/data/lire-filtered.parquet
runs/**/data/lire-filtered-with-letters.parquet

# Compile output from R/Stan/NIMBLE installs — large, noise, reproducible
